WHY A SEPARATE LICENCE

MIT grants rights over "the Software" and does not map cleanly onto a dataset. This
repository is roughly half data by value, and it is a dataset about the European
Union, where a substantial database also attracts a sui generis extraction right
under Directive 96/9/EC that MIT does not address at all. CC BY 4.0 explicitly
licenses those rights and makes attribution unambiguous.

Attribution matters here for a specific reason. This dataset groups named states by a
published rule over sourced findings, and every fact carries the evidence behind it.
Requiring attribution keeps each finding traceable back to its source, its checks and
its caveats instead of circulating as a bare fact.

